{"name":"China Seas","hex":"#034f7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"China Seas","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A series of marginal seas in the Western Pacific Ocean around China, including the Yellow Sea, the East China Sea and the South China Sea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/China_Seas"}],"entries":[{"title":"China Seas","blocks":[{"text":"The China Seas consist of a series of marginal seas in the Western Pacific Ocean, around China. They are the major components signifying the transition from the continent of Asia to the Pacific Ocean. They have been described in terms of their collective vastness and complexity:"},{"text":"The four seas of China, the Bohai Sea, the Huanghai Sea, the East China Sea, and the South China Sea, occupy a total area of about 4.7 million sq. km, half of the area of Mainland China. These seas are located in the southeastern margin of the Eurasian continent and subject to the interactions between the Eurasian, Pacific, and Indian-Australian plates. The seas have complicated geology and rich natural resources."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Seas","wikidata":"Q398805"},{"title":"China Seas (film)","blocks":[{"text":"China Seas is a 1935 American adventure film starring Clark Gable as a brave sea captain, Jean Harlow as his brassy paramour, and Wallace Beery as a suspect character. The oceangoing epic also features Rosalind Russell, Lewis Stone, Akim Tamiroff, and Hattie McDaniel, while humorist Robert Benchley portrays a character reeling drunk from one end of the film to the other."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/China_Seas_lobby_card_2.jpg/330px-China_Seas_lobby_card_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Seas_(film)","wikidata":"Q319147"},{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China","wikidata":"Q148"},{"title":"List of seas on Earth","blocks":[{"text":"This is a list of seas of the World Ocean, including marginal seas, areas of water, various gulfs, bights, bays, and straits. In many cases it is a matter of tradition for a body of water to be named a sea or a bay, etc., therefore all these types are listed here. Entities called \"seas\" which are not divisions of the World Ocean are not included in this list, nor are ocean gyres."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Oceans_and_seas_boundaries_map-en.svg/330px-Oceans_and_seas_boundaries_map-en.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_seas_on_Earth","wikidata":"Q229088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/China_Seas_lobby_card_3.JPG/500px-China_Seas_lobby_card_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/China_Seas_lobby_card_3.JPG/1280px-China_Seas_lobby_card_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign